From 7b351fb01936a2356dec6688f9f5855fe37fd082 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quim T <26749475+espetro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:55:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: make default routing path codegen-free and
 runtime-portable

Replace all new Function codegen on the default route registration and
lookup paths with semantically equivalent closures and precomputed
checkers:

- node.js: match every multi-char static prefix with String#indexOf
  instead of a compiled charCodeAt chain
- handler-storage.js: interpret the per-node param-object builder and
  constraint bitmask matcher from precomputed {mask, store, mustMatch}
  triples instead of generating code

This makes the whole default (non-compile()) path free of runtime code
generation, which is required for AOT-compiled runtimes such as
vercel-labs/scriptc and for strict-CSP environments. Router.compile()
remains available as an opt-in codegen path.

Additional portability fixes, all semantics-preserving:

- parse with try/catch new URL() instead of the URL.parse/URL.canParse
  feature-detect (same null-on-bad-input contract everywhere)
- load safe-regex2 optionally so runtimes without it degrade to
  allowUnsafeRegex-style behavior instead of crashing on require
- parse querystrings with node:querystring and move fast-querystring to
  devDependencies (it is only needed by the custom-parser test)
- replace instanceof/new.target checks and object/module shorthand
  forms that not all runtimes lower
- iterate httpMethods by index instead of for-in + hasOwnProperty

Verified: eslint clean, borp 554/554, tstyche 58/58 under Node;
throughput parity with the previous revision on the repo's workload.
